hi i'm keanu and this is my recipe for a  fork flavored cheesecake  [Music]  this recipe is a total throwback to my  childhood back in elementary school we  had these magazines where you could  order christmas gifts for people and  they had this poor flavored cheesecake  where it was four individual cheesecakes  cut up into quarters but all put  onto  one piece of cardboard and i figured i  could probably try to make it all in one  pan  so what made this cheesecake a bit  tricky is that i wanted to divide up  four very liquidy fluid items the thing  that made the most sense to me was to  use ingredients that were already in a  cheesecake so i opted for graham  crackers so once i got through the  structural part of the recipe the next  challenge was the four flavors  cheesecakes are really fun because you  can flavor them with whatever you want  but each different flavoring component  has its own chemistry so each cheesecake  batter end up having its own texture and  consistency so i had to play around with  every single flavor to make sure one it  tasted really good because end of day  doesn't matter what a dessert looks like  if it does not taste good it doesn't  really matter and then also that it was  thick enough where once i put it in its  corner it didn't budge stayed put  but it was still like nice and creamy  once it was all set  when it came to choosing flavors the  number one obvious one was chocolate  i love chocolate everyone loves  chocolate and chocolate hazelnut spread  is really thick and creamy so i knew  once i fold it into the cheesecake  batter is going to be really thick and  would fold up now the other flavors not  so easy the second flavor i wanted to go  with was lemon because it's a non-baked  cheesecake i think lemon is a really  good bright fresh flavor it's like very  summery and it's honestly one of my  favorites so i use lemon curd because if  i put in lemon juice it would have been  way too runny and then i just added a  little bit more lemon curd on the top to  make it visually pleasing the third  flavor i used was  just for the plain jeans in the world  everyone needs something simple so i  just did a vanilla cheesecake but to  give it like a little bit more oomph and  make it just as pretty as everything  else i added some raspberry jam vanilla  berries classic combination so i just  swirled in the top to make it very  pretty and then added some fresh berries  on the edge  now the fourth and final flavor  [Music]  me  it the fourth and final flavor was meant  to be caramel but the consistency of  that varied  so much between every product i use some  were super runny some were so thick i  couldn't even fold them in and it was  really tough when i was testing this  recipe i thought the cheat cake was done  it was beautiful and then as we're  filming the beauty shots the caramel  completely fell apart it literally was  oozing out of the side of the pan  because there's way too much water in it  but our lovely friends in brazil have  created a great food product called  dolce de leche which has a very similar  taste to caramel but it's so smooth and  thick so once i figured to use that it  was smooth sailing from there  and all the flavors  were good to go  i wanted people to have the option of  having that like prized double flavor  slice of cheesecake where you cut a  quarter inch of what's on the left and  quarter on the right and you have like a  two for one special however i think all  the flavors go really well together but  i had to check so i tested double  forkfuls of all the flavors just to see  what went and the only one that really  didn't go too well was a lemon curd and  chocolate so in the final cheesecake i  put them on opposing ends and then  everything else was good from there  the most struggling part about  developing this recipe  was to make it simple i wanted to be  like very all levels friendly  it's easy to make things complicated  it's difficult to make them simple it's  my philosophy of recipe development this  video didn't take long at all to do  wow  took like a day  full play the cheesecake  cool
 

